\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Dynamical MLR from this work. \emph  {Panel (a):} mass as a function of $M_{\mathrm  {G}}$ at $Z=-0.6,-0.3,0,+0.3$ (solid lines, shaded bands: posterior credible intervals), compared with PARSEC at the same metallicities (dashed lines), \citet  {Hwang2024DynamicalMasses} (dash-dotted), and literature masses: eclipsing binaries (Xiong et al. 2023), visual orbits \citep  {Mann2019}, Gaia orbits plus SB2 \citep  {Chevalier2023}, and asteroseismology \citep  {Serenelli2017}. \emph  {Panel (b):} mass relative to PARSEC at $Z=0$. The solid line is the posterior median of this work, and the grey band is the systematic uncertainty from the shape of $p(\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle u$}\mathaccent "0365{u})$, spanned by the MLRs obtained with eccentricity indices $\alpha _e=1.0$ and $1.5$ around the adopted $\alpha _e=1.23$ (Sect.~\ref {sec:sys_pu}). Literature points with a measured metallicity are shown only if it is within $0.15$\,dex of the solar value on their own scale; the masses of Chevalier et al. have no metallicity and are shown unfiltered.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
